STEP 3A -- the authored precondition applied VERBATIM refuses every read (finding O-9)  done
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Method: before supplying anything, the authored steps 4 and 5 were run against the
  authored configuration exactly as written, to record what it actually does on this
  platform.

  A1 = authored step 4, authored expectation "Can get 1.3.6.1.2.1.1.5 info":

box$ /usr/bin/snmpget -On -t 3 -r 1 -v 3 -u TESTtestTESTtestTEST -l authPriv -a MD5 \
       -A <PASS len=20 sha1=0eeef6a537> -x DES -X <PASS len=20 sha1=a587e0b9da> \
       10.38.22.34 1.3.6.1.2.1.1.5.0
  | .1.3.6.1.2.1.1.5.0 = No Such Object available on this agent at this OID
  RESULT NOSUCH                          <-- authored step 4 would FAIL here

  A2 = authored step 5, authored expectation "Cannot get 1.3.6.1.2.1.2.1 info":

box$ /usr/bin/snmpget ... 10.38.22.34 1.3.6.1.2.1.2.1.0
  | .1.3.6.1.2.1.2.1.0 = No Such Object available on this agent at this OID
  RESULT NOSUCH                          <-- authored step 5 "passes", but vacuously

  Both reads are refused, so the authored precondition as written can demonstrate
  nothing: it denies EVERYTHING, and the include/exclude discriminator the case exists to
  test has no contrast left in it. The refusal is NOT a credential problem -- neither
  reply is an authentication error, so the MD5 digest and the DES decryption both
  succeeded at the agent and the group matched. The denial is view access: the group's
  read view name resolves to nothing, and a view that is undefined permits no OID.

  The one missing line was supplied, and nothing else:

awplus# configure terminal
awplus(config)# snmp-server view MOSTmostMOSTmostMOST 1.3.6.1.2.1.1 included
awplus(config)# end
awplus# show snmp-server view
  SNMP view information:
    View Name ............... MOSTmostMOSTmostMOST
      OID .................... 1.3.6.1.2.1.1
      Type ................... included
    View Name ............... system
      OID .................... 1.3.6.1.2.1.1
      Type ................... included

  The added view carries exactly the subtree the authored `system` view carries, under
  the name the authored group actually reads. The authored group, user, host and `system`
  view are untouched. swi_d.cfg is this configuration, and it is what every graded step
  below was measured under.

  => STEP 3A done, and recorded as finding O-9 (a defect in the TEST CASE, not in the
     platform): AWPTCM-T43870's precondition is internally inconsistent -- the group
     reads view MOSTmostMOSTmostMOST, the block defines only a view called `system`, and
     nothing ever defines MOSTmostMOSTmostMOST, so applied verbatim every read is refused
     and authored step 4 fails. Supplying that single line makes all nine authored steps
     behave exactly as authored, as the steps below show. Secondary: the step-6 OID is
     typed `1.3.6.1.1.2.1.1.5`, which is not a path to sysName -- step 7 and the case's
     own OID glossary say `1.3.6.1.2.1.1.5`. Recommended fix to the case: rename the view
     in the configuration block to MOSTmostMOSTmostMOST, and correct the step-6 OID.

