  The accepted syntax, read off the DUT's own parser with a read-only help probe:

awplus(config)# no snmp-server view ?    -> <cr>      (no OID argument is accepted)
awplus(config)# no snmp-server user ?    -> <cr>
awplus(config)# no snmp-server group ?   -> <cr>

  Recorded as observation O-10 (PLATFORM CLI): `snmp-server view <name> <oid>
  {included|excluded}` is per-OID, but `no snmp-server view <name>` takes only the name
  and deletes the WHOLE view -- there is no way to withdraw a single OID entry from a
  view; it must be deleted and rebuilt. The same shape applies to `no snmp-server user
  <name>` and `no snmp-server group <name>`.

awplus# configure terminal
awplus(config)# no snmp-server user TESTtestTESTtestTEST
awplus(config)# no snmp-server group ADMINadminADMINadmin
awplus(config)# no snmp-server view MOSTmostMOSTmostMOST
awplus(config)# no snmp-server view system
